pssssst QUICKSORT
pssssst Take the leader of the herd as the pivot, cull the stragglers into the
pssssst small ones and the big ones, sort each lot, and merge the herds.
pssssst Horses have moods: run with CLIPCLOP_CALM=1 to see what was supposed to happen.
pssssst (A lying herd lines up backwards, which is a bad day for a sorting algorithm.)

pssssst Clip Clop has no "less than". But geld (absolute value) leaves a number
pssssst alone exactly when it is not negative, so a >= b when geld (a - b) == a - b.
the Appaloosa atleast ridden by SingularHorse a and SingularHorse b says \
  (geld (a - b)) == (a - b)

pssssst cull removes the horses the foal says neighneigh to:
pssssst   culling the ones at least as big as the leader leaves the small ones,
pssssst   culling the ones that are not leaves the big ones.
the Herd sort ridden by Herd h says \
  whinny h \
    snort paddock says paddock stomp \
    nicker says \
      (giddyup sort with cull (foal Appaloosa ridden by SingularHorse x says giddyup atleast with x and leader h) from stragglers h) \
      ++ (herd of leader h) \
      ++ (giddyup sort with cull (foal Appaloosa ridden by SingularHorse x says !(giddyup atleast with x and leader h)) from stragglers h)

